# Dependencies
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
node_modules/
**/node_modules

# Benchmark/eval fixture-seed lockfiles are install artifacts (their package.json +
# node_modules are ignored too); keep them untracked so dependabot does not scan
# stale fixture deps. Real MCP-server lockfiles elsewhere stay tracked + scanned.
**/seed/package-lock.json

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Database files
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Generic database patterns
# ───────────────────────────────────────────
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite3

# ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime state folders (plugin / tooling state)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Publish each folder and its README to external users, but ignore the
# machine-specific runtime data inside. The contents-glob (…/**) ignores the data
# WITHOUT excluding the directory, so the README negations below are honored. A
# bare directory-exclude (trailing slash) would block descent and hide the README.
# The **/ prefix also covers nested runtime-mirror copies of these folders.
**/.advisor-state/**
**/.smart-router-telemetry/**
**/.completion-sentinel-state/**
**/.goal-state/**
**/.loop-guard-state/**
**/.spec-gate-state/**
!.opencode/skills/.advisor-state/README.md
!.opencode/skills/.smart-router-telemetry/README.md
!.opencode/skills/.completion-sentinel-state/README.md
!.opencode/skills/.goal-state/README.md
!.opencode/skills/.loop-guard-state/README.md
!.opencode/skills/.spec-gate-state/README.md

